{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#436","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#436","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#436\",\"parent_revision\":\"f17842ba3be3a02609690d498900d508cc03617f7a1217eab18b01e6e2ebbc7c\",\"root_revision\":\"f17842ba3be3a02609690d498900d508cc03617f7a1217eab18b01e6e2ebbc7c\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThe research-curator skill needs an MCP server that integrates the notebooklm-py library (https://github.com/teng-lin/notebooklm-py) to enable the research curator agent to access Google NotebookLM research systems. This would allow creating notebooks, adding sources, generating audio overviews, and querying NotebookLM content programmatically as part of the research curation workflow. Use /fastmcp-creator to build the MCP server inside the research-curator skill directory. Success: research-curator agent can create/manage NotebookLM notebooks and use them as research sources via MCP tools. Verification: MCP server starts, tools are callable, and NotebookLM operations complete successfully.\\n\\n## Fact-Check\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**Claim 1**: notebooklm-py library exists and enables creating notebooks, adding sources, generating audio overviews\\n- verdict: VERIFIED\\n- claim: The library provides programmatic access to NotebookLM\\n- evidence: PyPI package notebooklm-py v0.3.4 exists; summary: 'Unofficial Python library for automating Google NotebookLM'\\n- source: https://pypi.org/pypi/notebooklm-py/json (accessed 2026-04-17)\\n\\n**Claim 2**: notebooklm-py is a proper API client suitable for MCP server integration\\n- verdict: REFUTED\\n- claim: Library integrates Google NotebookLM programmatically via API\\n- evidence: Package requires playwright>=1.40.0 (browser automation). Summary explicitly says 'automating' not 'API client'. This is browser automation, not a stable REST/gRPC API.\\n- source: PyPI metadata, requires_dist field (accessed 2026-04-17)\\n\\n**Claim 3**: GitHub repository https://github.com/teng-lin/notebooklm-py exists\\n- verdict: INCONCLUSIVE\\n- claim: Library source is available for review\\n- evidence: URL provided but not fetched during this session\\n- source: Item description (unverified)\\n\\n**Claim 4**: MCP server can start, tools can be called, and NotebookLM operations complete successfully\\n- verdict: INCONCLUSIVE\\n- claim: A FastMCP server wrapping notebooklm-py would be functional\\n- evidence: Success requires Playwright browser installation, valid Google account authentication, and stable UI. None of these are verified for the target environment.\\n- source: notebooklm-py PyPI dependencies (accessed 2026-04-17)\\n</div>\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nRT-ICA Snapshot: Create NotebookLM MCP server in research-curator skill\\nDate: 2026-04-17\\nGoal: Build a FastMCP server wrapping Google NotebookLM so the research-curator agent can create/manage notebooks and use them as research sources.\\nConditions:\\n1. notebooklm-py library exists on PyPI (v0.3.4, beta, Development Status 4) | Status: AVAILABLE\\n2. notebooklm-py is an UNOFFICIAL library using Playwright browser automation \u2014 not a Google API | Status: AVAILABLE\\n3. Library requires playwright>=1.40.0 (browser automation, not HTTP client) | Status: AVAILABLE\\n4. research-curator skill directory exists at .claude/skills/research-curator/ | Status: AVAILABLE\\n5. No existing MCP server in the research-curator skill directory | Status: AVAILABLE\\n6. fastmcp-creator skill available for building MCP servers | Status: AVAILABLE\\n7. Playwright requires browser installation (playwright install chromium) and may not work headless in CI | Status: DERIVABLE\\n8. Google NotebookLM official public API existence | Status: MISSING\\n9. Authentication mechanism: notebooklm-py requires Google account login via browser | Status: DERIVABLE\\n10. Whether MCP server wrapping browser automation is stable enough for agent use | Status: MISSING\\nAVAILABLE count: 6\\nDERIVABLE count: 2\\nMISSING count: 2\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-17)\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\nP1 \u2014 useful enhancement to research workflow. Blocked on design decision: browser automation is fragile; item should be held until Google releases an official API or the team consciously accepts browser automation risk.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- [ ] Design decision made: browser automation approach accepted OR item deferred until official Google NotebookLM API releases\\n- [ ] If browser automation: FastMCP server script exists at `.claude/skills/research-curator/scripts/notebooklm_server.py`\\n- [ ] If browser automation: Playwright dependency documented with install instructions\\n- [ ] If browser automation: Authentication strategy defined and implemented (Google credentials)\\n- [ ] MCP server starts and lists tools via `fastmcp list --command 'uv run ...'`\\n- [ ] At minimum, these tools callable: create_notebook, add_source, list_notebooks\\n- [ ] SKILL.md frontmatter updated with `mcp:` block pointing to the server\\n- [ ] research-curator agent can reference and use the NotebookLM tools\\n- [ ] Error handling for authentication failures and API unavailability\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- notebooklm-py from PyPI (v0.3.4)\\n- playwright browser installation\\n- Google account with NotebookLM access\\n- /fastmcp-creator skill for server scaffold\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nM \u2014 FastMCP server scaffold is quick via /fastmcp-creator. Main complexity is browser automation setup, auth flow, and environment reproducibility. If official API becomes available, effort drops to S.\\n\\n### Agent Instructions (instruct AI to use current interface)\\n\\n- `.claude/skills/research-curator/SKILL.md` \u2014 orchestrator needs to know NotebookLM tools exist\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Consumers (read the changed interface)\\n\\n- `.claude/agents/research-curator.md` \u2014 if it exists; would need to be updated to use NotebookLM tools\\n- `plugins/` research-curator agent files \u2014 need to reference new MCP tools\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Other References\\n\\n- None identified.\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Producers (write the changed interface)\\n\\n- `.claude/skills/research-curator/` \u2014 new MCP server script to be added here\\n- `.claude/skills/research-curator/SKILL.md` \u2014 needs MCP server reference added to frontmatter\\n\\n### Configuration / CI\\n\\n- Any `.mcp.json` referencing the research-curator skill would need updating\\n- CI would need `playwright install chromium` added to setup if tests run the MCP server\\n\\n### Description\\n\\nBuild a FastMCP server inside the research-curator skill that wraps the notebooklm-py library, enabling the research-curator agent to create/manage Google NotebookLM notebooks programmatically as part of its research workflow.\\n\\n**Critical design constraint discovered during grooming**: notebooklm-py v0.3.4 is an unofficial library using Playwright browser automation, NOT a Google API client. It requires:\\n- Playwright browser installation (`playwright install chromium`)\\n- A Google account with NotebookLM access\\n- Browser automation that is vulnerable to UI changes\\n\\nGoogle has not released an official NotebookLM API as of 2026-04-17. This design decision (browser automation vs waiting for official API) must be resolved before implementation begins.\\n\\n### Documentation (will become stale)\\n\\n- `.claude/skills/research-curator/references/` \u2014 no existing NotebookLM documentation; new reference file needed\\n\\n### Ecosystem Completeness Checklist\\n\\n- [ ] Design decision: browser automation vs wait for official API\\n- [ ] Authentication strategy defined (Google account, credentials storage)\\n- [ ] FastMCP server implementation\\n- [ ] SKILL.md updated with MCP server reference\\n- [ ] Playwright installation documented\\n- [ ] Tests written for the MCP server tools\\n\\n### Impact Radius\\n\\n\\n\\n### Issue Classification\\n\\n**Type**: unbounded-design\\n**Rationale**: No Google NotebookLM official API exists. The only available library (notebooklm-py v0.3.4) uses Playwright browser automation. Building an MCP server on top of browser automation introduces unstated dependencies (browser installation, Google account auth flow, UI stability) that are not bounded by the item description. The technical approach requires a design decision before implementation can proceed.\\n**Analysis Method**: design-framing\\n**Scenario Target**: Research-curator agent needs persistent knowledge storage and retrieval \u2192 NotebookLM via browser automation, OR official API when released, OR alternative stable knowledge backend\\n\\n### Systems Inventory\\n\\n- `.claude/skills/research-curator/` \u2192 skill directory (target location)\\n- `notebooklm-py` PyPI package \u2192 dependency\\n- `playwright` \u2192 transitive browser automation dependency\\n- Google NotebookLM web UI \u2192 automation target\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **create notebooklm mcp server in research-curator skill** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: User request\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-03-05\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"0a12def37da12d091152dc0b24697218988b1c12bdc9f7d990ef31086778cfad\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPTCA3w\"}"}